WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
- That's right, it's our
Barbie Dream Hour, everybody.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.010
I am Dark Diva Barbie, you're welcome.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:05.843
And what would it be

00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:08.400
without the cast of the huge, enormous,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.950
upcoming blockbuster movie "Barbie"?

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.010
The movie opens in theaters
everywhere, July 21st.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.570
Everybody, please give it up

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.920
for Margot Robbie,
(engine revving)

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.803
Issa Rae, Kate McKinnon, America Ferrera.

00:00:19.872 --> 00:00:24.872
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:44.854 --> 00:00:47.851
(Kate screaming)
(Kelly murmuring)

00:00:47.851 --> 00:00:50.550
I'm so excited you're here.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.779
We even dressed alike, too.

00:00:52.779 --> 00:00:55.168
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:55.168 --> 00:00:57.163
(guests murmuring)

00:00:57.163 --> 00:00:59.760
Give it up, have a seat, ladies.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.990
Oh my gosh, that was
the best entrance ever.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.640
- I felt like I was selling
a car on a game show.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.473
- Yeah, you were like, did you-

00:01:06.473 --> 00:01:07.980
- I was like-
- Vanna White.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:08.850
Yes, it was nice.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.520
Her leg was over the
door, it was very classy.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.020
Well, welcome back to Margot.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.340
America, y'all been on this show before.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.350
But welcome to the show, ladies.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.215
- Thank you so much.

00:01:17.215 --> 00:01:19.230
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.730
- It's such an incredible cast
of women, and men as well.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.980
But last time you were here, you said...

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.720
Kind of, they're all right.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.710
But you said you were gonna learn,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.510
I think it was French and banjo.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.280
Have you started at all?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.583
- No, Kelly, it's been a
busy year and my New Year's-

00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:38.040
- [Kelly] I've been
learning Spanish for 20, so.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.260
- My New Year's resolutions
got pushed aside

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.080
and I'm still looking for a banjo teacher.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.470
Remember we spoke about that.
- Margot, I'm ready for ya!

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.490
- Jaco could teach you.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.083
He just is busy a lot.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.186
His boss is crazy.

00:01:51.186 --> 00:01:53.010
(audience applauding)

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.500
But your mom, Issa, was a teacher, right?

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.820
- Yeah, my mom was a French teacher

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.130
so she could help you with the
New Year's resolution, yeah.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:01:58.963
- [Kelly] Look!

00:01:58.963 --> 00:02:00.300
- [Margot] My resolutions
are back on track now.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.620
- I got you, she got you.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.090
I volunteer her.
- Her mom, Jaco,

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.860
between that, you have got this covered.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.910
- No excuses anymore.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.352
- But no, I love that
your mom was a teacher.

00:02:09.352 --> 00:02:10.890
My mother was a teacher as well.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.340
Did you ever feel like you
would go in that field at all?

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.173
Me, no.

00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:16.837
- Yeah, no, I think, yes, seeing her-

00:02:16.837 --> 00:02:18.930
- I like my kids, not y'all's (chuckles).

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.820
- It was just too much
and then, even watching...

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.740
We used to do "Take Your
Daughter To Work Day."

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.810
I used to visit her and that was fun.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.770
But, kids are terrible, so I don't...

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.840
Thank God, she didn't teach at my school,

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.330
she taught at my younger siblings' school.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.500
And so, they had it way worse.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.914
So I had a healthy distance from it.

00:02:36.914 --> 00:02:38.460
- (chuckles) That's amazing.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.560
Yeah, I don't think my mom
taught at mine, ever, either.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.350
We have loved you like on
SNL, everything you do.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.940
- What?
(audience laughing)

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.060
- I have literally seen you
so much in my household.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.350
Because Melissa lives next door to me

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.650
and your "Ghostbusters"
is my son's favorite.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.120
I've seen it a billion times.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.460
I feel like we're friends, it's awkward.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.500
But, anyway, I love you-
- I'm a lifelong fan.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.000
I am actually, a lifelong fan.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.530
This is big.
(Kelly chuckling)

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.820
This is really big for me, you guys.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.560
- No, so, I'm just a huge fan.
- I'm flustered.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.480
- I'm wondering though,
'cause you're so funny

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.313
and I wonder with people

00:03:07.313 --> 00:03:08.820
that are on SNL, did you grow up

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.003
in a hysterical family? Was
everybody funny in your family?

00:03:11.003 --> 00:03:12.720
Did you grow up watching a lot of comedy?

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.753
- Hysterical, sure.
- How are you this funny?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.420
- Yeah, my parents
actually, are very funny

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:23.010
and they used to quote SNL all the time.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.990
Like, "We are from France," and, "Oh, no,"

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.520
and all these early SNL quotes

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.670
that I just thought were English phrases.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.820
And so, I would say to my
teacher, "We are from France."

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.830
And she would be like, "Are you well?"

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.056
Or you know, that kind of thing.

00:03:36.056 --> 00:03:36.889
(everyone laughing)

00:03:36.889 --> 00:03:39.810
So, it was very much in
the culture of the home.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.940
- I love that, what a
great home, that's fun.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.773
- I was awesome.

00:03:42.773 --> 00:03:45.540
- Were they freaking out
when you made it onto SNL?

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.373
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:46.373 --> 00:03:47.430
- [Kelly] I was gonna say they probably-

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.391
- Not as much as me.

00:03:48.391 --> 00:03:49.620
- (chuckles) Yeah.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.620
- 'Cause then, I had to be
on SNL and I was scared.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.453
- It's hysterical.

00:03:53.453 --> 00:03:54.720
Well do people still come up

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.820
to you and ask for any kind of impression?

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.493
- They do.

00:03:58.493 --> 00:03:59.527
I was asked recently,

00:03:59.527 --> 00:04:01.290
"When are you gonna do
Justin Bieber again?"

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.160
And I was like, "It's not funny anymore.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.350
He's a consummate professional.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.404
He's a man of God with
a healthy marriage."

00:04:09.404 --> 00:04:10.997
- He got (beep) together (chuckles).

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.230
- Yeah.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.230
- That's hysterical.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.500
- My favorite character is the one

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.360
that I actually got to
do the sketch with you

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.630
when you're playing the
oldest starlet with the-

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:25.140
- Oh, yeah, you were sweet
to participate in that.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:25.973
- [Margot] That's like one

00:04:25.973 --> 00:04:27.240
of my favorite characters
you've ever done.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.590
And I got to see it firsthand.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.423
- Oh, man!

00:04:29.423 --> 00:04:31.324
- It's so funny.
- That's nice, she's...

00:04:31.324 --> 00:04:32.157
(audience applauding)

00:04:32.157 --> 00:04:33.960
- So America, did you know any

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.460
of these women before filming?

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.040
- No, I didn't know Margot at all.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.350
Issa, maybe we said hi at events.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:42.702
- We were on a whole panel
together, America, it's fine.

00:04:42.702 --> 00:04:44.835
(everyone laughing)

00:04:44.835 --> 00:04:46.823
I wasn't memorable or
anything, that's fine.

00:04:46.823 --> 00:04:47.656
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:47.656 --> 00:04:49.110
- That was qualifies as an event, Issa!

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.360
- That is like a real
friend that calls you out.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.612
- The one in Boston?

00:04:53.612 --> 00:04:54.551
The one we-
- So, now you know the-

00:04:54.551 --> 00:04:57.664
- No, I do remember but that, okay, yeah.

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.497
See, okay, but there's-

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:01.770
- She's like, "Wrong
answer, I knew everyone."

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.180
- But this is my problem

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.250
because actually, my story about Kate is

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:09.630
that I saw her at an event

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:10.470
and I thought, "Oh, my god,

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.450
that's Kate McKinnon,
I have to go say hi."

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.440
And I walked up

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.190
and I was like, "Kate,
I am your biggest fan."

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:22.140
And she's like, "America,
you don't remember?"

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.423
And I was like, "Oh no, what?"

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.940
But you went by a different last name.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.773
- Sure.

00:05:27.773 --> 00:05:28.606
- And when we were

00:05:28.606 --> 00:05:29.970
in high school, we both both attended

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:34.290
the same drama summer program
at Northwestern University.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.340
And it was like one of those moments

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:38.280
in the movie where your
mind rewinds quickly

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.050
and forward and then things make sense.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:43.560
And I go, "You're Kate, you're funny Kate.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:47.190
You're the funniest person
that was at the camp

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:49.620
and also, the funniest person
I'd ever met to that date,

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.150
and of course, you're Kate McKinnon!"

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.840
- But I remember it
'cause America was in...

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.860
We all had our separate shows, right?

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:59.430
And America did the most
amazing dramatic monologue

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:02.010
and everyone was like,
(groans), "America."

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:04.444
And I was like, "Oh my God, America."

00:06:04.444 --> 00:06:06.133
And I played a bug in my show.

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:07.093
(everyone laughing)

00:06:07.093 --> 00:06:07.926
And so-

00:06:07.926 --> 00:06:08.759
- But it was the funniest bug ever.

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:10.200
- [Kate] It's okay that
you didn't remember me.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.831
- I'm just gonna not be offended
when I see America tomorrow

00:06:12.831 --> 00:06:14.981
or something and she's
like, "And you are?"

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:17.843
- But as a joke, I-
- It's okay,

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.310
you forget everyone, it's okay.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.930
- As a joke, I should've been
like, "Welcome to the show,

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:22.763
you've never been here."

00:06:22.763 --> 00:06:24.600
- The truth is last night, I tried

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.610
to envision what this was gonna feel like.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.260
And I thought, "If little America knew

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.690
that she was standing or sitting next

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.523
to these four people

00:06:31.523 --> 00:06:35.310
who I truly, deeply,
deeply admire and idolize,"

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.180
I was crying

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.694
in bed last night thinking
about this moment.

00:06:37.694 --> 00:06:39.177
- [Kate] Aww, that's nice.

00:06:39.177 --> 00:06:40.113
- So this is like a dream and this is-

00:06:40.113 --> 00:06:41.534
- It's a dream cast for sure.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.660
- This is what making the movie felt like,

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.580
it was like how...

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:45.600
It's a dream.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.470
- I love that.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:48.600
So Margot, is it true
that you had a sleepover

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.800
for the cast, before the movie?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.423
- We had a Barbie sleepover.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.290
It was as fun as it sounds.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.440
It was Greta's idea.
- You're welcome, cast.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.370
- Yeah, it was Greta's
idea, I can't take credit.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.630
We all went to Claridge's

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.720
which is a really
gorgeous hotel in London.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.750
We all shared beds and wore our pajamas

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.510
and ordered room service and played games

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:13.116
and found out that America
is exceptionally competitive.

00:07:13.116 --> 00:07:14.070
(everyone laughing)

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.800
- I am extremely competitive
and nobody told me

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.840
that it was a sexy Barbie sleepover.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.750
So everybody was in really
pretty, silky nightgowns.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.583
And I was

00:07:22.583 --> 00:07:26.460
in the most grandma, floral,
twin set you could imagine.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.740
- She somehow simultaneously,
looked like an old lady

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.620
but a five-year-old at the
same time, it was the cutest.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:32.520
And she's so teeny-

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:33.900
- While she's yelling
at you during the game?

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:37.020
- While she's screaming at
you, but it was so charming.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.090
I mean she was like
the cutest little thing

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.830
you'd put a toddler in and go to bed

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.150
and then she was rousing at us

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.621
for not knowing the rules, so it was-

00:07:43.621 --> 00:07:45.204
- If they're not gonna play-

00:07:45.204 --> 00:07:47.448
- If you're not gonna
compete, why are you here?

00:07:47.448 --> 00:07:49.500
- If you're not gonna do it.
- Why play?

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.660
Margot, another of your
Kens was Ryan Gosling.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:53.793
So what was it like to work
with him? He's so talented.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.840
- Again, as amazing as it
sounds, he is just, woo!

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.343
- [Kelly] He's funny, man.

00:07:59.343 --> 00:08:01.786
He's got very funny, comedic timings.

00:08:01.786 --> 00:08:06.060
- He is the most comedically gifted actor.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.830
I think he's just so known as being

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.570
such a brilliant dramatic actor

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:10.560
that people are sometimes

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.640
like, "Oh yeah, he is really funny.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.720
He was funny in that thing."

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.140
In this movie, he's funny on
a completely different level.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.520
I ruined all his takes

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.590
'cause I just laughed through them.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:22.140
I actually, now watch the edit of the film

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.060
and I can see Greta cutting away

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.940
before I laugh and my
corners of my mouth are like,

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.310
and then she cuts back to him
'cause I've started laughing.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:30.960
- 'Cause he's so serious,
but it's so funny.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.220
- 'Cause he's so funny.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.750
- Oh, and I agree.
- He's going for it

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.130
in this movie, it's amazing.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:37.230
- Issa, Margot, so you guys,
y'all have a dance scene

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.063
in the movie?

00:08:38.063 --> 00:08:38.896
How was that?

00:08:38.896 --> 00:08:40.770
It was so good, I saw it, actually.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:42.488
- Yeah, was it?

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.321
(audience laughing)

00:08:43.321 --> 00:08:44.430
- You're amazing!

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.870
- You know, it was my first day.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.180
The dance sequence happened my first day,

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.473
it was like I landed.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.357
They told me that it was gonna
be a dance sequence in it.

00:08:54.357 --> 00:08:57.150
And I was like, "Oh, cool, that
has nothing to do with me."

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:01.833
And then, they sent me the
footage to rehearse it.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.260
I had something that I was doing in D.C.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.540
and I had to learn it in 24 hours,

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.310
and the cast had been
already working on it.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.530
And so I was like, "This is
literally my worst nightmare.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.880
I'm not a dancer."

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.440
So I tried to learn the routine,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.273
I was with my friends.

00:09:14.273 --> 00:09:16.380
They were like, "Girl, get
it, one, two, one, two.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.120
Get it, one, two, three, four."

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.350
And then when I landed, they were

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:22.350
like, "Oh, the dance is
completely different," (laughs).

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.240
So then I landed,

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:28.500
my first day meeting the cast
was doing this dance number

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.333
and it was-

00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:31.910
- What a way to break the ice.
- Yeah, way to break the ice

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:36.139
in my face, yes, my pride,
my ego but, you know.

00:09:36.139 --> 00:09:37.980
- I'm bummed you didn't get
to do the dance rehearsals

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.990
with us 'cause that was
honestly the funnest part

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.670
of prepping this movie is doing...

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.490
We do dance rehearsals
for probably two weeks.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.080
This, definitely, was
why it was so stressful

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.670
for you 'cause you
didn't get the two weeks.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.857
But we'd all go and I'd been doing it

00:09:49.857 --> 00:09:51.150
for a week on my own,

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.500
and I was like, "Ooh, this is so fun,"

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.605
'cause it's like the kinda dancing you do

00:09:54.605 --> 00:09:56.130
with a hairbrush in front of your mirror

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.350
when you're a kid, so it's
like silly, fun, dancing.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.200
But, then the other Barbies
all started arriving

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.510
for the dance rehearsal
and then I was like...

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:04.710
My ego went through the roof

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.000
'cause they're like, "Yeah!"

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.560
Everyone's screaming and clapping

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.760
and then, we'd do it all together.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:09.900
And then we'd get everyone

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.750
before shooting, we'd get
out whole crew and everything

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.850
to do a little dance warmup together.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:15.683
And it was so fun,

00:10:15.683 --> 00:10:17.770
just the vibe the rest of the
day would be, just amazing.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:18.990
- Well, I don't know if you know

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.360
but, Drew, I mean, you guys rehearse too.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.730
I know that y'all dance. I
know that you can dance it out.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:25.140
You wanna show some moves?

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.630
Were you wanting to show
us some moves, guys?

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.920
Why you backing up?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:30.433
Why you backing up?

00:10:30.433 --> 00:10:34.273
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:10:34.273 --> 00:10:37.035
Are you doing Kid 'n Play?

00:10:37.035 --> 00:10:39.618
(upbeat music)

00:10:46.243 --> 00:10:49.942
(audience applauding)

00:10:49.942 --> 00:10:50.775
Oh my God.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.440
My favorite part was your restart.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.855
You were like, "No, we didn't get it."

00:10:57.855 --> 00:10:59.030
- From the top, a one, two, three, four.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:00.390
- From the top.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:04.050
You can tell the year you
were born by that dance alone.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.950
It was the same year as me (chuckles).

00:11:08.033 --> 00:11:09.410
- [Margot] That was impressive-

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:12.300
- We have an impressive crew, 11 Emmys.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:13.515
They got nominated, 11 Emmys.

00:11:13.515 --> 00:11:17.622
(everyone cheering and applauding)

00:11:17.622 --> 00:11:20.040
- Also, we have a very
impressive audience.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.962
Everyone's dressed up amazingly.

00:11:21.962 --> 00:11:23.760
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.040
- So Margot, can you explain
the story of the movie?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:30.180
- Well, Barbie Land is perfect

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:34.260
and the Barbies are having
perfect day after perfect day.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.790
And everything's just wonderful

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.610
in Barbie Land unless, you're a Ken

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.070
or until you have an existential crisis,

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.690
which my Barbie does.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.040
- What about the rest of you?

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:44.970
Who's your Barbie?

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:45.803
America, you can start.

00:11:45.803 --> 00:11:47.940
- I'm not a Barbie, I mean, I am a Barbie

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.260
'cause we're all Barbies.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:51.360
Unless you're a Ken,
then you're not a Barbie.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.620
But, I'm a human in the movie, I think-

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:56.940
- Because there's Barbie.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.767
- There's Barbie Land.
- Barbie Land, and then what?

00:11:58.767 --> 00:12:01.248
- And in the last trailer
you kind of see the hint

00:12:01.248 --> 00:12:04.920
of Barbie and Ken are headed
toward the real world.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.030
And in the real world,

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:10.140
my character, Gloria, encounters Barbie

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:15.140
and it's a connection and
high jinks ensue from there.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.480
And I think that's all
I'm allowed to say, right?

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.310
- And then, I don't
wanna spoil everything,

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:21.143
who's your Barbie?

00:12:21.143 --> 00:12:21.976
Who do you play?

00:12:21.976 --> 00:12:24.600
- Did you guys ever have a
Barbie like the one Barbie

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.840
that you designate as like her,

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:30.780
where you cut their
hair, burn their clothes

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.610
and draw on them?

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:36.780
That's the one I play.
(America laughing)

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.870
- Because let's face it,
we all had one (laughs).

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:41.820
You're like, "What if I colored her hair?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:42.957
She needs a haircut."

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:45.120
I love your Barbie.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:46.050
Can you do the splits

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.030
in real life or did they have to like?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.840
- I can go to about there

00:12:51.168 --> 00:12:53.820
and then, the whole system breaks down.

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:54.653
I can't do a split.

00:12:54.653 --> 00:12:57.297
- Oh my God, way to go, then
the editing job is incredible.

00:12:57.297 --> 00:12:59.670
- No, they did this whole technical thing

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.633
where my legs are always at a 180.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.090
- Who's your Barbie, Issa?

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.906
- My Barbie is president of Barbie Land.

00:13:08.906 --> 00:13:09.990
(everyone cheering and applauding)

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.910
- [Kelly] You're very funny.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.706
- Thank you!
- Hysterical.

00:13:13.706 --> 00:13:14.539
- Thank you, so much.

00:13:14.539 --> 00:13:15.930
- Yeah.
- Yeah, it was a treat

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.515
to be president somewhere.

00:13:18.515 --> 00:13:21.515
(everyone laughing)

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:25.140
- What would you do if
you really were president,

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:26.403
funny or serious?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.805
- Serious, healthcare for
sure, everywhere, university.

00:13:31.805 --> 00:13:35.190
(audience applauding)

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.900
Funny, I would be more selfish,

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.580
I could just eat everywhere for free.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.730
That would be my taxes.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:43.050
Yeah, just walk in
anywhere, anybody's house.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:46.171
If I like your cooking,
you have to cook me a meal.

00:13:46.171 --> 00:13:47.571
- I'm president.
- Yeah, I'm president.

00:13:47.571 --> 00:13:48.404
- I'm having dinner.
- Are you gonna feed me?

00:13:48.404 --> 00:13:49.680
Yeah.
(everyone laughing)

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.590
- Well America, and Margot,
Barbie is such an iconic toy.

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:55.260
So how does it feel, I don't know,

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.460
to bring her story to life?

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.590
I played with Barbies when
I was a kid, did y'all?

00:13:58.590 --> 00:13:59.700
- Yes.
- I did not.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.140
- You did not?

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:02.880
- I was not a Barbie player.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.808
Were you guys Barbie?
- I was.

00:14:04.808 --> 00:14:07.368
- It wasn't cool to, but
I still did, secretly.

00:14:07.368 --> 00:14:08.610
(America chuckling)

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:09.443
- [Kelly] What'd you say?

00:14:09.443 --> 00:14:11.070
- It wasn't cool to play with Barbies.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.020
It was like at school
you'd be like, "Barbies?"

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:14.643
And then at home I'd be like...

00:14:14.643 --> 00:14:16.327
(everyone laughing)

00:14:16.327 --> 00:14:17.583
"You kiss," yeah.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.390
- I don't remember having my own Barbies,

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:22.740
but my cousin had a box of them.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:25.173
They were like all her Barbies.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.440
We would cut the hair
and do all that stuff.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.900
But I got the fold-out house one Christmas

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:34.320
when I was young and I was obsessed,

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:37.170
the Dreamhouse that folded out.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:39.150
Honestly, coming into this movie,

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:42.240
that was such a priority, was the sets

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.379
and then getting to
see them be built right

00:14:44.379 --> 00:14:45.390
in front of us

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:48.030
and they were just
huge, real life versions

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:48.935
of the Dreamhouse.

00:14:48.935 --> 00:14:51.390
- It looks incredible.
- It was so amazing

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.400
and it's so beautiful.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:54.399
- [Kelly] Our department says that.

00:14:54.399 --> 00:14:55.232
- And it was like the first thing I said

00:14:55.232 --> 00:14:57.030
to Greta you know, when
we first sat down, talked

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:57.863
about the movie,

00:14:57.863 --> 00:15:00.240
I was like, "I'll follow your vision,

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:03.090
whatever you want this Barbie
movie to be, let's do that.

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.280
Except I just have one favor.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.190
Please, please, please,
can we have a dream house

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.630
where she has a slide that goes

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.040
from her bedroom down to her pool?

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.450
'Cause that is my goal in life."

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.907
And she was like, "Yeah, sure."

00:15:15.791 --> 00:15:16.624
- [Kelly] That's your thing?

00:15:16.624 --> 00:15:18.290
- "That's your thing?" And I
was like, "Yes, that's it."

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:19.500
- Not like your character arc.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:21.593
She probably thought you were
going big like ugh, okay.

00:15:21.593 --> 00:15:23.100
- Or even the tone of
the movie, none of that.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.170
I was just like, "I just
want that slide so bad."

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:28.050
- Oh my God, I think I'm
older than all of you.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:29.880
So I loved...

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.560
I was obsessed with Barbies.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.721
It was the cool thing
whenever I was a kid.

00:15:33.721 --> 00:15:35.320
- But it's so different now-
- So you thought...

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:39.060
- Back then, I mean, to
be perfectly honest, one

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:39.900
of the reasons I didn't play

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:43.680
with Barbies, 'cause I
didn't feel reflected

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:45.540
in the world of Barbie, you know?

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.900
It was a very Americana version of beauty.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.480
And, maybe there was one Black Barbie

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:52.890
and there were white Barbies

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.350
but now, it's totally different.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.820
And to be invited,

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:58.560
to get to be a part of this narrative

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:03.360
where Barbie represents
so many more people, is

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:07.320
like it's the Barbie we deserve, you know?

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.940
It's so moving to get to be a part

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.480
of this re-imagining
of this world of beauty

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:15.660
and fun and aspiration where
more of us get to be seen.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.690
- Absolutely, it's cool too

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:19.950
when you have kids,

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.163
'cause it's come back
around in such a big way.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.980
My little girl, her friends,

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.810
they all have Barbies, they're obsessed.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.390
Every time, she's like, "I
want the car, I want the Jeep."

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:31.940
I'm like, "Wait for a holiday."

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.640
Not Tuesday, you don't get it every day.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.890
But anyway, it's really cool
though, to see her playing

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.110
and doing the same stuff that
I did whenever I was a kid.

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:41.790
But yeah, it's cool to see your kids.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:42.930
I wonder if your kids will get into it,

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:44.997
but my daughter's really into Barbies.

00:16:44.997 --> 00:16:46.350
And when I walk in, girl,

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:48.977
she's got 'em kissing
just like you just said.

00:16:48.977 --> 00:16:52.230
I'm like, "What is Barbie and Ken doing?"

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:53.190
She's like, "They were kissing.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:54.269
Mom, get out!"

00:16:54.269 --> 00:16:56.850
(everyone laughing)

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.770
Did did you play with Barbies,
were you into Barbies?

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:01.404
- I was Barbie-curious,
there were Barbies.

00:17:01.404 --> 00:17:03.360
- (laughs) You were Barbie adjacent?

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:05.190
- There were Barbies in the home,

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:08.943
my sister had a lot of Barbies and they,

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.850
they had diagnoses.

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:16.850
I mean, these Barbies were
messed up at her hand, you know.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:20.190
But they were there and she spent hours

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:22.260
with her friends doing the most...

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:24.420
I mean, it was like her
training as a comedian

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:27.900
and a theater artist, she came up

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.190
with all these amazing things

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.930
and built an entire world out of them.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:33.600
And I thought, "Wow, that's really cool.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.010
You're really cool."

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.200
I love my sister, I'll say it here.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.873
- [Kelly] I'll say it here right now.

